    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature on `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`. Salutation = `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added an optional `title` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (editable input), constrained to the enum `MR/MRS/MS/DR` per spec.\n   - Added a read-only derived `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persistent `title` column with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `salutation` mapping expression (`title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when title is null/blank). MapStruct auto-maps the DTO's `TitleEnum` \u2194 the entity's `String` title.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL change was required).\n\nThe `salutation` is derived on read in the mapper (consistent with existing derived fields like `displayName`/`initials`), so no new OfficeFloor function steps were needed \u2014 the existing `BuildOwner` \u2192 `SaveOwner` \u2192 respond pipeline persists `title`, and the GET pipeline's responder renders the computed `salutation`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `salutation = \"DR who\"`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
